From 8390cdd97e4629e31951c8c290f2cd3a29ab6018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wrysk <wrysk@wryskware.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:15:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add semantic profile version 5: size-aware permission for
 paid hunter growth

Experiment branch only, based on the reviewed diagnostic 0d867f1 so the bounded
mutation-site ledger is reused rather than rebuilt. Implements the single
candidate in astra-hunter-size-aware-growth-proposal-2026-09-13.md. This is an
experiment selector, not an accepted biological default.

At the existing post-oxidation, pre-growth site the permission threshold becomes
growth_reserve_min * reserve_max * clamp(structure / structure_adult, 0, 1) for
authoritative members carrying version 5, and stays exactly the old expression for
ordinary organisms and for versions 3 and 4. FixedHunterProfile::growth_gate is
the whole production change; a degenerate adult denominator returns the legacy
gate rather than propagating a NaN, since a NaN gate would silently read as a very
strict threshold instead of the mechanism under test.

Version 5 explicitly keeps charge80's fixed 0.80 E_max oxidation activation. That
is the trap the proposal names: matching only version 4 in oxidation_policy would
have dropped the charging policy and made this two changes. lanternjaw_trial still
writes version 3, and an unsupported version is still refused by name rather than
reinterpreted.

The gate is a precondition and nothing else. The increment keeps all four caps,
both debits, the construction heat and the physiological ordering; nothing is
capped to reserve minus gate and no reserve floor is protected.

The flow ledger adapts to a moving gate: the overwritten gate_reserve scalar is
renamed gate_reserve_last and joined by min, max, the legacy gate beside it, and
the threshold and size at the first actual growth, plus first-growth and
first-adult boundaries and max structure. A member that never grew reports None
rather than a fabricated threshold.

hunter_compare gains reserve-targets-charge80-size-gate-v1 and a --seeds filter
for a pilot; a restricted run records ran_seeds and seed_subset_pilot in its
manifest so a partial collection cannot be read as a cohort.

Tests: cubarium-core 152 lib plus every integration suite, 0 failures, including
16 new in hunter_size_gate covering the selector, the gate values at S=.8/1.2/1.6/2,
strict-equality refusal and the next representable reserve, degenerate denominators,
all four increment caps with real positive growth and closing debit identities, zero
build cost, mid-growth snapshot restart against an uninterrupted run, old-reader
refusal, and observer inertness. hunter_compare 78, including the recipe's profile
diff and unchanged founder inventory.

Two existing expectations were updated because their subject genuinely changed:
SUPPORTED_PROFILE_VERSIONS is now [3, 4, 5], and the unsupported-version example
moved from 5 to 6. A member's juvenile_growth_rate is in the profile's positive
validation set, so the proposal's zero-rate case is unreachable for a member; that
is pinned as a contract refusal and the limiting arithmetic is covered at 1e-9
instead.

