From ae866a556a9d7032963cf80a8f4574f9f5611929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wrysk <wrysk@wryskware.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:34:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Wire the bounded flow ledger into hunter_compare

Closes the named gap from the seed-1 handoff: the runner recorded structure only
at 200-tick census boundaries, which bounds when a change is first seen and cannot
show a per-tick transaction, its binding cap or the gate it crossed.

Each arm now enables the ledger after its post-initialization snapshot and writes
one flow.json at close. It is one record per member for the whole run plus
fixed-width bins, never a per-tick world dump: a member that died is retained with
its removal-site stocks and one alive at the horizon is right-censored, so
birth/death same-tick and last-interval accounting survive. The records carry
source-specific intake, the actual post-oxidation gate as a range with the
threshold and size at the first growth, the binding cap of every step, and the
reserve, battery and heat each increment paid.

FlowLedger::validate is the run's gate and the reducer's. It fails the arm on a
member the arm knows it held but the ledger did not record, on a record for an
unregistered member, on any non-finite or negative amount, on payment
reconciliation judged against the ledger's own frozen 1e-9 tolerance rather than
one supplied by a reader, on structure built without matching reserve spent, and
on a first-growth boundary that disagrees with whether anything was built. The
arm also records whether it reached the planned horizon.

Observer neutrality is checked in-run: before the ledger is switched on, each arm
steps its own opening twice for 2000 ticks, with and without recording, and the
run fails unless the state hash and every event record agree. That is a bounded
prefix; the full-horizon statement comes from comparing this build against the
earlier pilot, which ran the identical recipe with no ledger in the loop.

No threshold, rate, cost, food or ecology changed. Original tolerances are
unchanged and the raw legacy energy diagnostic is untouched and still not an audit.

cargo test -p cubarium-core: 153 lib (one new for validate) plus every integration
suite, 0 failures. cargo test --example hunter_compare: 78, 0 failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
